  "body": "LOT-071 (docs lot). Sets the LOT-071 row of `docs/LOTS.md` to `done (#27)`.\n\n**Problem.** Q-4 kept AQ on condition of a first-use notice, and ADR 0007 left third-party endpoints \"decided per feature\", but no document listed the third-party hosts, what each receives, who runs it or what the user is told. LOT-055, LOT-056, LOT-083 and the Phase 4 GIF work need that list.\n\n**Cause.** The legacy app spreads third-party calls across the code: AQ (`aq.super-h.fr`, including an RSS fetch at every launch with no user action), Chevereto rehost (`img3.super-h.fr`), the Giphy SDK, video player iframes, and images from any host a poster chose, private addresses included, loaded as soon as the page is shown.\n\n**What changed.**\n- `docs/lots/LOT-071-third-party-services.md`: inventory T1–T8 (trigger, data sent, owner, lot, status), with legacy file:line citations @ `2440d79` and the image hosts seen in the topic captures; rules R1–R6 (no forum cookie or `Referer` to third parties, keys and base URLs as configuration, no analytics SDK, inventory = allow-list); first-use notices N1–N4; operator decisions of 2026-10-27: **D-071-1** images, option C (private/LAN hosts, numeric host spellings and non-image `*.hardware.fr` paths never loaded; third-party images on tap or per the FEAT-011 setting), applied by LOT-083; **D-071-2** video players: placeholder, player on tap; **D-071-3** AQ: badge and check as legacy, notice before the first creation. R3, R5, R6 and N1–N3 are proposed, applied unless the operator objects.\n- `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md` §8: a pointer to the spec and a row for the video players.\n- `docs/LOTS.md` capture backlog: one row for the `reho.st` Referer check (§7 E26) and an `http`-only image host over https.\n\nOnly these three files change: the services themselves are implemented by their own lots.\n\n**Tests.** None, because this is a docs lot with no code. markdownlint (MD051, MD056) and `scripts/check-lot-deps.py` pass locally.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CHteTFWfkJGeSNGpSW\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added guidance on third-party services, including image and video loading behavior, request handling, and first-use notices.\n  * Documented supported video players and identified several legacy players.\n  * Marked the third-party-service inventory as complete and added image-fetch scenarios to the capture backlog.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
